            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>In a real space that includes a user 120, predetermined rules are used to set boundary surfaces of a play area 184 in reference to boundary surfaces 182a and 182b of the field of view of an imaging device 12.If the user gets out of the play area 184, a warning state determining section determines that there is a need for a warning and superposes a warning image on a display image. A direction in the real space or the state therein, for example, is used to determine whether or not margin areas are to be set between the boundary surfaces of the play area 184 and the boundary surfaces 182a and 182b of the field of view, or how wide the margin areas are to be.</p>
            </abstract>
